## Biographies
Agnes E. Thorarinsdottir was born in Akureyri, Iceland, in 1993. She received a B.S. in Chemistry from the University of Iceland in 2015 and a Ph.D. in Chemistry from Northwestern University in 2019. At Northwestern, she worked under the supervision of T. David Harris in the fields of molecular magnetism, magnetic coordination polymers, and bioresponsive magnetic resonance imaging probes. She started her postdoctoral position in the lab of Prof. Daniel G. Nocera at Harvard University in January 2020.
T. David Harris was born in Poca, West Virginia, in 1981. He received a B.S. in Chemistry from Marshall University in 2004 and a Ph.D. in Chemistry from the University of California, Berkeley, in 2010. After carrying out postdoctoral research at Harvard University, he joined the faculty at Northwestern University in 2012. In 2019, he moved to the University of California, Berkeley, as a project scientist. His research is focused on the synthesis and study of inorganic molecules and materials, with an emphasis on metal−organic magnets and magnetic resonance imaging probes.
